Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:01:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] =?UTF-8?q?zcloudium:=20web=20essentials=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20SSH-only=20remote=20workspaces,=20staged=20attachments,=20wo?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rking=20MCP=20settings?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. /ws/remote/:id exposes the complete remote channel set (the same
   ProxyChannel.toService service proxies RemoteServiceAccess builds) instead
   of four services; the remote connection is disposed when the browser socket
   closes, and POST /api/dispose-remote/:id releases an attached connection.
   Ticket ids come from randomUUID. Web platform.connectRemote drives the
   upstream HTTP contract: POST /api/connect-remote, WS attach on the ticket,
   renderer-side session registration with the resolved target.

2. The remote wizard offers SSH only in web: Docker and WSL connect to the
   machine running the client, which only the desktop has (isDesktop gate).

3. POST /api/stage-attachment writes uploaded bytes into the agent's own
   space ({dataRoot}/tmp/paste-attachments/YYYY-MM-DD, dir 0700, file 0600 —
   the desktop temp-text writer's layout) and returns a real agent-readable
   path. The web platform's createTempTextAttachment uses it, and the composer
   stages binary files that have no inlinable content, so zip/docx/... become
   real files instead of a send-time failure. The 20 MiB protocol cap stands.

4. MCP settings work in web: the platform's load/save delegate to the
   server-side mcp-sync channel (already exposed to web clients), which
   reads/writes the agent's own ~/.zcode/cli/config.json atomically.
