From e1ea46dd3c8c8a0bdf3ee38b933f2cffb27569c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZCloudium <zcloudium@local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:19:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] zcloudium: pass the remote-asset deploy options on web
 connect-remote

Desktop builds inject their release-assets CDN URL at compile time,
which is why SSH connect worked there out of the box; the server bundle
has no such define, so /api/connect-remote called the deploy with empty
CDN options and it refused ('production remote assets require...').
The route now passes what desktop passes: env override
ZCODE_REMOTE_ASSET_CDN_BASE_URL first (same contract), otherwise the
pinned ZCodium release assets, and a cache dir on the server's own data
volume (private via the entrypoint umask, persistent across restarts).
